  "question": {
    "text": "A mass $M$, attached to a horizontal spring, executes S.H.M. with amplitude $A_1$. When the mass $M$ passes through its mean position then a smaller mass $\\mathrm{m}$ is placed over it and both of them move together with amplitude $A_2$. The ratio of $\\left(\\frac{A_1}{A_2}\\right)$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sxzjS",
      "text": "\n $\\frac{M+m}{M}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UdMud",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{M}{M+m}\\right)^{1 / 2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z4OoC",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{M}}\\right)^{1 / 2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PgZBX",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{M}{M+m}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Energy of simple harmonic oscillator is constant.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{2} M \\omega^2 A_1^2=\\frac{1}{2}(m+M) \\omega^2 A_2^2 \\\\\n& \\frac{A_1^2}{A_2^2}=\\frac{M+m}{M} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\frac{A_1}{A_2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{M+m}{M}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
